            <ArticleTitle>Back pain: medical evaluation and therapy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>163-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Most patients with acute low back pain or sciatica improve with appropriate conservative therapy, and most require no immediate diagnostic studies beyond a careful history and examination. In patients with &quot;red flags&quot; for visceral, malignant, or infectious causes or possible cauda equina syndrome, a more aggressive evaluation is mandatory. In patients whose pain does not respond to initial management or who have chronic symptoms, diagnostic re-evaluation is appropriate.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
